        "text": "Now let me look at the newer dated 商业模式 file (20260817) to understand the latest 段永平 perspective format. Wait — the task says the 商业模式 file is outdated, and there IS a dated one: `001316润贝航科-商业模式-段永平视角-20260817.md`. Hmm, interesting. The task says:\n\n2) 读旧文件 reports/001316润贝航科-商业模式-段永平视角.md（商业模式 视角，内容已过时）\n3) 重写 reports/001316润贝航科-商业模式-段永平视角.md，使其与其他三份最新报告的结论对齐\n\nSo there is actually a newer dated file (20260817) for 商业模式 too. But the task explicitly says to rewrite the OLD file (without date suffix) and align with the other three new reports. Let me check the new dated 商业模式 file — the task's instruction in step 1 says \"同视角若存在带 -YYYYMMDD 日期后缀的新文件和旧文件，优先读带日期后缀的新文件\" — this applies to the three files in step 1 (which exist as dated). For step 2, it says read the OLD 商业模式 file specifically.\n\nHmm, but there's a dated 商业模式-20260817 file too. The task says read the old one and rewrite the old one. Should I also read the dated one? The task is explicit: rewrite the OLD file (无日期后缀) to align with the other three NEW reports. The task doesn't mention reading the new 商业模式 dated file. But to be thorough and understand context, let me read it anyway — it may help me understand what the \"new\" 段永平 view was in round 19, and the alignment target. Actually, wait — the task says the old file's 内容已过时 and should be rewritten to align with the other three new reports. The new dated 商业模式 file exists and presumably already IS aligned (round 19). But the task wants the OLD file rewritten. Interesting — maybe the user wants the old file (without suffix) to be the canonical one for this perspective.\n\nLet me read the new dated 商业模式 file to see what round 19 said, since it will inform the rewrite. But the key requirements are:\n1. Align with the three new reports (巴菲特, 芒格, 李录)\n2. Keep 段永平's analytical stance/methodology\n3. End with \"## 量化结论\" section with exactly 5 lines in the specified format\n\nKey data points to align from the three new reports:\n- 现价: 26.60 元 